  "oneLinerQuestion": "Determine how many car fleets will arrive at a target destination.",
  "url": "https://leetcode.com/problems/car-fleet/",
  "explanation": "Sort cars descending by start position. For each car, compute arrival time = (target - pos) / speed. If a trailing car's arrival time <= leading fleet's arrival time, it catches up and merges into that fleet.",
  "pseudoCode": "FUNCTION carFleet(target, position, speed):\n    pair = [[p, s] FOR p, s IN ZIP(position, speed)]\n    SORT(pair BY position DESCENDING)\n    stack = EMPTY_STACK()\n    FOR p, s IN pair DO:\n        PUSH (target - p) / s TO stack\n        IF LENGTH(stack) >= 2 AND TOP(stack) <= SECOND_TOP(stack) THEN POP(stack)\n    END FOR\n    RETURN LENGTH(stack)\nEND FUNCTION",
